</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><source><italic>Mycobacterium bovis</italic> Infection in Animals and Humans. 2nd ed</source><publisher-loc>Boston, MA</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Blackwell publishing</publisher-name><fpage>18</fpage><lpage>33</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005478-Andersen1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Andersen</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Munk</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Pollock</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Doherty</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Specific immune-based diagnosis of tuberculosis.</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>356</volume><fpage>1099</fpage><lpage>1104</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11009160</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005478-Palmer1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Palmer</surname><given-names>MV</given-names></name><name><surname>Waters</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name><name><surname>Thacker</surname><given-names>TC</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Lesion development and immunohistochemical changes in granulomas from cattle experimentally infected with <italic>Mycobacterium bovis</italic>.</article-title><source>Vet Pathol</source><volume>44</volume><fpage>863</fpage><lpage>874</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18039899</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005478-Song1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Song</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Bandow</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Sherman</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Baker</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></na